Source: Psychological Practice App Requirements — Version 1.0 — September 2026

Link & Heal — Full Product & Technical Blueprint Page 2
1. Product Vision & Boundaries
Link & Heal connects what happens inside therapy sessions with structured between-session activity. The central
loop is: assign → complete → organize → review → discuss → measure progress.
Non-negotiable principles
• Privacy first: features that conflict with privacy are redesigned or removed.
• Client simplicity: routine actions such as mood should take about 60 seconds or less.
• Clinical value: collected data should appear as a useful chart, alert, summary or clinical view.
• Therapist control: the therapist decides what each client tracks and sees.
• Professional boundaries: messaging, if enabled, is not an emergency channel.
• Safety: risk workflows must not depend only on a therapist noticing a notification.
Product is not
• An AI therapist, social network, dating app or gamified wellness product.
• An emergency-response service.
• A replacement for therapist clinical judgment.
• An EHR/telehealth-first platform; future integrations are supported by the architecture but are not required for Phase
1.
2. Platforms & Main Surfaces
Surface Users Purpose
Client mobile app Clients / partners / teens / family members Mood, assessments, homework, goals, progress, resources, consent and privacy
Therapist mobile app Therapists Alerts, client review, pre-session view and quick actions.
Therapist web dashboard Therapists / authorized admin roles Full management, analytics, libraries, reports and configuration.
Backend API All roles Authentication, authorization, business rules, scoring, notifications, synchronizat
Database + private storage System Clinical data, metadata, files and immutable audit records.
Client requirement: iOS and Android from one codebase plus therapist web. The source document mentions Flutter
or React-based native development; the exact framework remains open.
3. Roles & Permission Model
Role Access
Therapist Own clients, clinical records for those clients, assignments, measures, homework, resources, alerts and reports.
Adult client Own data and assigned work.
Couple partner Own private data plus explicitly shared couple content.
Teen Own data; guardian access only where explicitly permitted.
Guardian Only allowed information; no detailed teen answers by default.
Family member Own data plus explicitly shared family content.
Admin assistant Administrative functions without clinical content.
Recommended rule: the UI is never the security boundary. Every API request must be authorized against identity,
role, therapist-client relationship, consent, visibility and resource ownership.
